  "body": "The old text associates “pick” with `<select multiple>` elements and “toggle” with other `<select>` elements <sup>[0]</sup>, but the defining instances of “pick” <sup>[1]</sup> and “toggle” <sup>[2]</sup> make the converse association.\r\n\r\n0. [“If the […]” in § 4.11.3.5 “Using the `<option>` element to define a command”](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#using-the-option-element-to-define-a-command)\r\n1. [“picked” in § 4.10.7 “The `<select>` element”](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#concept-select-pick)\r\n2. [“toggle” in § 4.10.7 “The `<select>` element”](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#concept-select-toggle)\r\n",
